The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and enhances antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express higher levels of the costimulatory molecule CD86 compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ). Panel B demonstrates the phenotyping of OVA-containing MigDCs, indicating that Nano-11 targets antigen to CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells. Panel C, through in vivo imaging, reveals that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide, maintains antigen at the injection site for several days, whereas soluble OVA rapidly clears, supporting Nano-11's role in sustained immune stimulation.